Owner aesthetic approval and physical-phone qualification remain open.

Original reference remodel (rear branding superseded by95): 110-degree opening, extruded rear square recesses,
metallic teal shell, convex lime controls, blue D-pad, rear-only supplied emblem,
clipped stylus and table-contact feet. Existing lamp/room/background unchanged.
One focused browser gate passes9cases in1.8m: four DS cases and five affected
GBA dock/branding/mobile-inspection cases. Actual motion samples prove no
GBA intersection; held-pointer canvas changes prove live inspection repaint.
Table cartridge separation, actual stylus geometry, material pixels and
console-specific dock restoration pass. Reviewed current desktop table,
front/rear, real Twin Lab and390px captures; refresh README screenshots.
25units,syntax,build,diff checks pass. No full-suite/device/owner approval claim.
Initialize DS storage before first shader compilation to retain the5s deadline.

Initial prototype evidence (historical, model superseded):
The separate turquoise/lime DS and stylus retain the GBA on the same table.
Pinned EmulatorJS4.2.3/DeSmuME directly boots the original BIOS-free Twin Lab
fixture. Real native frames reach both physical LCDs; button and lower-screen
stylus input reach the core. Separate browser databases and checksummed
.bbds-save backups preserve system/ROM identity. Console switching checkpoints
and pauses the inactive runtime; power-on cold boots, while page reload plus
same-ROM selection resumes its checkpoint.
Final tests/browser/ds.spec.mjs run: three cases pass (57.2s), including native
and physical pixels, inputs, export/import, GBA coexistence, pause isolation,
cold boot, real reload recovery, 390px framing and CDN-error retry/reduced motion.
Six affected GBA regression cases and both cartridge viewport cases pass across
separate focused runs; this is not a full-suite or single eleven-case run.
Final npm test:25pass; npm run check and npm run build pass. Details and limits
are in docs/VERIFICATION.md; instructions and actual captures are in README.md.
No commercial compatibility, physical-phone performance, owner approval,
commit, deployment or new published edition is claimed.

